\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lift up your heads, ye gates of brass,
\par Ye bars of iron, yield,
\par And let the King of Glory pass ;
\par The Cross is in the field.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Ye armies of the living God,
\par His sacramental host,
\par Where hallowed footstep never trod,
\par Take your appointed post.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Though few and small and weak your bands,
\par Strong in your Captain's strength,
\par Go to the conquest of all lands ;
\par All must be His at length.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O fear not, faint not, halt not now;
\par Quit you like men, be strong ;
\par To Christ shall every nation bow,
\par And sing with you this song :
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Uplifted are the gates of brass ;
\par The bars of iron yield ;
\par Bohold the King of Glory pass !
\par The Cross hath won the field.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

